# SEO SUPER BOOSTER (this project)

Follow the full spec in **`SEO-SUPER-BOOSTER.md`** at the repo root. That file is the source of truth; this rule highlights how it maps here.

## Stack

- **Astro 7**, `output: 'static'`, HTML-first (no client-rendered indexable content).
- **Single locale:** `en-US` only — no hreflang, no i18n routing.
- **Domain & checkout:** `src/config/site.ts`, `astro.config.mjs` `site`, `src/config/checkout.ts` + `checkout-redirects.mjs`.
- **Per-page SEO:** `src/config/pageSeo.ts` + `resolvePageSeo()` in `src/config/seo.ts`.
- **Head / canonical / OG:** `src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro`.
- **JSON-LD:** `src/utils/schema.ts` via `JsonLd.astro`.
- **Commercial link attrs:** `src/config/affiliate.ts` (`rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"` on `/go/` links).
- **Sitemap:** `@astrojs/sitemap` + `src/config/sitemap.ts` (no `priority` / `changefreq` in output).

## Non‑negotiables

- Never fabricate reviews, forum users, stats, or pricing; use `TODO:` + list in report if content is missing.
- One primary keyword per URL; unique title, description, `<h1>`, canonical on every indexable page.
- Affiliate/commercial links: `rel="sponsored nofollow noopener"`; visible disclosure from config before the first such link on the page.
- Forum content is **editorial Q&A**, not fake users/posts (see SEO doc §5.1).
- Multi-pass verify before calling work done (SEO doc §13); run `npm run build`, `npm run check`, `npm run seo:audit` when changing SEO-facing code.

## Before large content or URL changes

Use the required-inputs checklist in SEO doc §1 (keywords, domain, affiliate URL, product features). Do not invent keywords or merchant URLs.
